meta {
  name: LLM Connectivity
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/health/llm
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

docs {
  # LLM Connectivity

  Health probe for the local-LLM advisory layer (app.llm.* / GET
  /api/llm/analyze). Checks that the configured runtime (Ollama by default, at
  app.llm.base-url) is reachable and that the configured model is installed.

  Uses a cheap /api/version + /api/tags probe — it does NOT run a generation, so
  it never cold-loads a model and is safe to poll frequently (unlike Webull
  Connectivity, which issues a real authenticated request).

  ## Outcomes
  - `200 UP`       — runtime reachable. `modelReady=true` means the configured
    model is installed; `false` adds a `warning` (the analyst would fail safe to
    WAIT until the model is pulled). Includes `version` and `latencyMs`.
  - `200 DISABLED` — app.llm.enabled=false; nothing is probed.
  - `503 DOWN`     — runtime unreachable; `detail` explains why. The app keeps
    running — the analyst just fails safe to WAIT until the runtime returns.

  Response always echoes `baseUrl`, `model`, `enabled`, and `timestamp`.

  ## Bringing the LLM up/down
  - Start : ./scripts/llm-start.sh
  - Stop  : ./scripts/llm-stop.sh
  - Status: ./scripts/llm-status.sh   (CLI equivalent of this probe)
}
